description: Guidance for event handlers if event-driven code is introduced.
---

# Event Handler Skill

No event bus, Kafka, RabbitMQ, saga, or outbox implementation is currently present.

Use this only if a task explicitly introduces event-driven behavior.

1. Confirm the chosen transport and existing project convention before implementing.
2. Make handlers idempotent with a stable event ID or business key.
3. Persist state changes before publishing follow-up events.
4. Add retry and backoff behavior appropriate to the transport.
5. Avoid publishing events from inside database transactions unless an outbox pattern is implemented.
6. Log handler failures with enough context to trace the event and affected aggregate.
7. Add focused tests around duplicate delivery and retry behavior when handlers are added.
